From 2831881cfd8c054d5e36daecb664d4478a62d014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@spark1.tail1a9513.ts.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: fix shared_guard policy and measure multi-stream
 shared/hold costs

Fix multi-stream shared drafting policy (100% lossless) so c4 decode sustains
uniform fixed-block drafting without graph-miss thrashing or single-stream vetoes:

- shared_guard.zig:
  - Enforce uniform shared draft depth for batched fixed-block drafters (minimizing
    verify_cache shapes to 1 key per depth), capped at TF_INKLING2_SHARED_MAX_ROWS
    (default 16, avoiding MoE tile=16 double-reads; 0 = uncapped).
  - Replace hard all-or-nothing 1.02 per-stream veto with aggregate throughput
    maximization (>1.01x plain) plus a softer per-stream floor
    (TF_INKLING2_SHARED_STREAM_FLOOR, default 0.85).
  - Probe d=2 on rounds 1-2 instead of round 16 so drafting starts by round 3,
    probe d=3 on rounds 24-25 when room permits, and refresh plain_ms at round 16
    after early stream divergence.
  - Dampen single-round graph-capture spike outliers in block_costs (alpha=0.04
    above 1.25x), rescale block_costs on sharp plain_ms divergence jumps so ratios
    stay anchored to measured ms, and use hold_costs + same-regime shared_costs
    priors.

- loop_backend.zig:
  - Measure diverged 4-stream verify costs at widths 12, 16, 24, 32 (using distinct
    token IDs per slot so MoE routing reflects real multi-stream divergence) and
    batched DFlash2 hold_costs at 1, 2, 4, 8 streams during warm(), plus lazy vs
    dense sampled head delta.
  - Persist extended costs in WarmRecord schema v2 (cache key inkling2-warm-v3)
    and export shared_costs + hold_costs in facts().

Credits (for NOTICE, Apache-2.0 / MIT):
- Shared fixed-block pricing and batched hold_costs concepts adapted from
  MiaAI-Lab (commit 9e3cf20b, patches 0006-mini-drafts.patch and
  0018-mini-dflash2-drafter.patch) and tonyd2wild (commit 2fe0eb57, patch 0018).
